<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <!--
    A-021 Phase 1 headless harness target (brief §10: "author the csproj so the
    headless target compiles exactly the API-free set; exclude GameLoop/
    RenderLayer/UIRoot from it").

    Two build facts about this NuGet SDK 8.0.425 csproj dialect are load-bearing
    and were verified by probe, not assumed:

    1. EnableDefaultCompileItems defaults to true, which implicitly includes
       EVERY .cs under the project directory. Declaring <Compile Include=...>
       on top of that is NETSDK1022 "Duplicate 'Compile' items" (a build
       failure, not a warning), and it also silently pulls the Unity-API files
       into the headless build. Hence the property is set to false here.

    2. With default items off, the <Compile> element's Exclude ATTRIBUTE works;
       the <Exclude> ELEMENT form is inert (it is treated as another include).

    The exclusion is provably real, not vacuous: GameLoop.cs / RenderLayer.cs /
    UIRoot.cs reference UnityEngine.* which does not exist in this toolchain, so
    if the Exclude clause ever stopped working the build would fail with CS0234/
    CS0103 rather than quietly pass. Brief §9 keeps those three files authored-
    per-contract but NOT compiled headless (no Unity toolchain in this
    environment).
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <EnableDefaultCompileItems>false</EnableDefaultCompileItems>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- A-023: Assets/Editor/BuildPlayerPackage.cs is the Unity Editor build
         script (UnityEditor API); it joins the excluded set so the headless
         targets keep compiling exactly the API-free sim surface. -->
    <Compile Include="Assets/**/*.cs"
             Exclude="Assets/Runtime/Bridge/Unity/GameLoop.cs;Assets/Runtime/Bridge/Unity/RenderLayer.cs;Assets/Runtime/Bridge/Unity/UIRoot.cs;Assets/Editor/BuildPlayerPackage.cs" />
    <Compile Include="tools/harness/*.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
